# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# /fde is the acronym people type, but it is a poor canonical path: the Wikipedia
# disambiguation page lists eleven meanings for FDE and "full disk encryption"
# outranks "Forward Deployed Engineer" for the bare acronym. So the spelled-out
# phrase is canonical and every short form 301s into it, which keeps the acronym
# usable in conversation without splitting ranking signal across two URLs.

/fde                      /forward-deployed-engineer/   301
/fde/                     /forward-deployed-engineer/   301
/forward-deployed-engineers  /forward-deployed-engineer/   301
/fde-resume               /forward-deployed-engineer/   301
/fde-jobs                 /forward-deployed-engineer/   301

# The panel Q&A lives at a spelled-out, question-intent path for the same reason:
# people and assistants search in phrases, not acronyms. The shorthand forms
# redirect in so they stay usable in conversation.
/fde-qna                  /forward-deployed-engineer/questions/   301
/fde-questions            /forward-deployed-engineer/questions/   301
/fde-panel                /forward-deployed-engineer/questions/   301
